---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getLocale, useTranslations } from '~/i18n/utils';

import Hero from '~/components/sections/Hero.astro';
import TrustBand from '~/components/sections/TrustBand.astro';
import MolarTv from '~/components/sections/MolarTv.astro';
import EducationLibrary from '~/components/sections/EducationLibrary.astro';
import UnderstandFirst from '~/components/sections/UnderstandFirst.astro';
import Everywhere from '~/components/sections/Everywhere.astro';
import Testimonials from '~/components/sections/Testimonials.astro';
import GrowthStory from '~/components/sections/GrowthStory.astro';
import SocialPlans from '~/components/sections/SocialPlans.astro';
import Faq from '~/components/sections/Faq.astro';
import FinalCta from '~/components/sections/FinalCta.astro';

import { faqSchema, productSchema } from '~/data/schema';

/*
	The home page sells MOLAR TV.

	One product, one price, one button, and the argument runs in a straight line
	from the fold to the checkout. Everything else on this page is either
	evidence for that or the upgrade path after it.

	Sections that used to run here and no longer do — none of them deleted, all
	of them still on their own pages:

	  Ecosystem       "the big idea", a five-armed diagram of the whole content
	                  ecosystem. It is a good drawing of a company; this page
	                  sells a $97 screen, and a systems diagram three sections in
	                  answers a question nobody has asked yet.
	  PatientJourney  the same ecosystem in six steps.
	  WhyMolar        six blocks of prose making the case a fourth time.
	  ProductSelector a "pick your product" grid under a page that has already
	                  shown every product.
	  ResourceHub     a wall of links off the page, at the point a visitor should
	                  be closer to checking out.
	  GlobalReach /
	  GeoBand         two adjacent bands on the same markets fact, which the flag
	                  band under the closing CTA now makes once.
	  ClientProof     grids of published posts, immediately above the same
	                  argument told better in the case study.
	  VideoReel       nine clips scrolling past under the bento wall that is
	                  already made of stills from the same nine.

	Two things here the strategy's own section list does not name, both
	deliberate:

	  Faq            it is linked from the Resources menu as /#faq, and
	                 netlify.toml redirects /faq to that fragment. The FAQPage
	                 structured data below is generated from the same array the
	                 section renders, so the two cannot drift.
	  productSchema  the plans are on this page with their prices visible, so
	                 Product/Offer markup describes something a visitor can see.
*/
const locale = getLocale(Astro);
const t = useTranslations(locale);
---

<BaseLayout
	title={t('pages.homeTitle')}
	description={t('pages.homeDesc')}
	ogImage={{
		src: '/images/og/home.png',
		alt: 'MOLAR TV — patient education for modern dental practices',
		width: 1200,
		height: 630,
	}}
	type="website"
	transparentNav
	schema={[productSchema(locale), faqSchema()]}
>
	{/*
		Order is the argument.

		  Hero              the offer, priced, with one button.
		  TrustBand         who already pays for it.
		  MolarTv           what it is — the screen, the channel, what is on it.
		  Everywhere        the three moments it runs in, right beside the section
		                    that just said what it is — moved up from after
		                    EducationLibrary/UnderstandFirst, by request.
		  EducationLibrary  what plays on it, as the real product UI. Still
		                    directly under MOLAR TV's own explanation per the
		                    09/01 brief, just with `Everywhere` between them now.
		  UnderstandFirst   why any of it matters — see it, understand it, trust
		                    the recommendation, say yes.
		  Testimonials      practices saying so on camera — one highlight, then two
		                    more. Back on the page and rebuilt around Vimeo embeds.
		  GrowthStory       the MOLAR Social case study, which is the upgrade this
		                    page earns rather than the thing it opens with.
		  SocialPlans       how much of it you want handled, at four prices.
		  Faq · FinalCta    the questions, then the ask.

		Testimonials before the case study is deliberate and it is a sequence, not
		a duplication: the films are practices saying the product works, and the
		case study is one account measured proving it. Voice, then evidence.

		`ContentShowcase` — "The work", a bento wall of seven category stills — is
		off this page. It sat at the point a visitor had already seen the product
		running on a screen, the library UI, and an account measured before and
		after. /our-work/ is the page for the work, and the case study links there.

		Everything after the plan grid is questions and the ask. By the time a
		visitor reaches the bottom the page should have left them with one thought
		— "I understand what MOLAR is, it is $97, I can try it free" — and every
		extra claim down there costs a fraction of that.
	*/}
	<Hero />
	<TrustBand />
	<MolarTv />
	<Everywhere />
	<EducationLibrary exploreCta={false} />
	<UnderstandFirst />
	{/*
		`filmsOnly`: the two cards under the highlight are films and a name, with
		no quotation. This section is a video wall here — the highlight carries the
		one quote worth reading, and a paragraph of prose under each small card
		made them top-heavy and competed with it. /patient-education/ runs the same
		component without the flag, because nothing there is filmed and the quotes
		are all it has.
	*/}
	<Testimonials filmsOnly />
	<GrowthStory />
	<SocialPlans />
	<Faq />
	<FinalCta />
</BaseLayout>
